{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T21:35:38Z",
  "_id": "wp-post-112933-en",
  "_rev": "Kra5TYIFOKLIQlRCd8Hj6V",
  "_type": "article",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-07-05T16:12:26Z",
  "author": {
    "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000000",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa is the place in Egypt where the word \"far\" really has meaning."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "4zhjw7h3kiv8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A long drive west from "
        },
        {
          "_key": "sifw2fxadk5a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "8wzdt81mnpej"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "1dtho39k9zlc",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", past "
        },
        {
          "_key": "2xug30qvnnjr",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "boq78g1dma0c"
          ],
          "text": "Marsa Matruh"
        },
        {
          "_key": "m7bi181zj9ij",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " on the Mediterranean coast, then south on desert roads. Inside dry land a basin appears holding date palms, olives, springs, and salt lakes. That is Siwa."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "8wzdt81mnpej",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "boq78g1dma0c",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58887",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000004",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Seeing this place only as a beautiful oasis isn't enough. Siwa is a land with culture and history different from Nile-valley Egypt. Most residents speak Siwi, an Amazigh-family language; architecture, craft, and social custom carry a layer different from the Nile-side."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "p76f1yqy9zy0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's appeal isn't one sight. The "
        },
        {
          "_key": "t269kydkp5x2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "aih8bgyr1gvh"
          ],
          "text": "Temple of the Oracle"
        },
        {
          "_key": "o73ogibnt9tl",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " of Amun that Alexander the Great sought, the salt-and-mud fortress town of Shali, the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "kqdjv7n7g601",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "r3lrp7hqmtwd"
          ],
          "text": "Mountain of the Dead"
        },
        {
          "_key": "29vx9o573svx",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", salt lakes, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "5n4a98ab8r0d",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "mkqmq1mxhl04"
          ],
          "text": "the Great Sand Sea"
        },
        {
          "_key": "3fcdi64b3v1s",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", date palm and olive fields. Their connection inside one small basin is Siwa's strength."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "aih8bgyr1gvh",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.siwa-oasis.temple-of-the-oracle",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "r3lrp7hqmtwd",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.siwa-oasis.mountain-of-the-dead",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "mkqmq1mxhl04",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.siwa-oasis.the-great-sand-sea",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What isolation kept"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's geography is history itself."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The oasis sits in a Western Desert depression close to the Libyan border. Surrounded by desert and salt lakes, exchange with the outside world has long not been easy. The isolation made life difficult and at the same time held the power to protect distinct culture."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's people are Egyptian nationals and culturally also tied to the North African Amazigh world. Siwi language, embroidery, silver jewellery, traditional wedding dress, and kershef architecture show distinctness well."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa wasn't fully cut off. Ancient Egyptian, Greek, Roman, Islamic, and modern-state influences reached this oasis in each era. Siwa didn't swallow them whole — it received them adapted to its land's conditions."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Temple of the Oracle of Amun"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What made Siwa famous in the ancient world was the Oracle of Amun."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The oracle temple sits at Aghurmi a little outside today's town. Not a fully preserved temple; the sanctuary space still reads. Stone has been worn by wind, the roof lost. Even so, the place's historical weight comes through."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In 331 BC, Alexander the Great, having taken Egypt under his rule, crossed the desert and visited Siwa. What he asked and what the oracle exactly answered differs in ancient sources. He did tie this visit to the legitimacy of his rule."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's oracle wasn't a mere provincial religious facility. A place where the Mediterranean world's powerful looked for political and religious endorsement. So however small the remains look, the meaning exceeds the scale."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Nearby are remains of the Umm Ubayda temple. Fragmentary; they show Amun worship at Siwa had roots before Alexander."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The ruins of Shali"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What makes the most striking scene at Siwa's centre is Shali."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Shali is a fortified town built from around the 13th century. The material is kershef, a local build mixing salt, mud, and clay. Strong in dry climate, thick walls eased heat, and the dense town protected residents from outside threat."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Old Shali was a fortress-like living space of narrow alleys and tall layered buildings. Residents lived inside, stored food, and prepared for the outside desert and unstable times."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Kershef is weak to water. In the 1926 heavy rains, salt-bearing walls collapsed and much of the town became unlivable. Residents moved down to the plain, and Shali remained as ruin."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Today's Shali isn't a perfectly preserved medieval city. A place collapsed, reinforced, and weathering little by little. Here you don't only see \"an old town\" — you see a city built from the land's material returning to the same land."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Climb up in the evening and Siwa's geography reads at once. Date-palm green, salt-lake white, the town's spread, the surrounding desert. As the first place to understand Siwa, Shali is very clear."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Gebel el-Mawta"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "On the town's north is Gebel el-Mawta — \"Mountain of the Dead\" — a burial hill."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Many tombs were cut into the rocky hill, mainly used from the 26th Dynasty into the Greco-Roman period. The Tomb of Si-Amun is especially known, with colour decoration remaining, showing Siwa, while isolated, still connected with the Nile valley and Mediterranean world."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6nocs1t3p3ru",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't expect "
        },
        {
          "_key": "qre77cixlusw",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "iz6v618zpm40"
          ],
          "text": "Valley of the Kings"
        },
        {
          "_key": "v001fx70y1ns",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " grandeur. A place to see Egyptian, Greek, and Libyan desert cultures layering inside individual tombs."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "iz6v618zpm40",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "From the hilltop, views of town and oasis. Siwa's cemetery isn't separated from life — it sits right next to town as part of the landscape."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Water, salt lakes, date palms"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The reason Siwa could exist is water."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Around the oasis are freshwater springs supporting date palms, olives, and gardens. The Spring of Cleopatra is one of the most accessible for travellers. The name became popular through tourism; no firm evidence the queen herself visited. As a springwater pool, easy to grasp, where you sense Siwa's water presence."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Salt lakes strongly mark Siwa's landscape. With high salinity, you float naturally entering. Known recently as photo spots; salt lakes are tourism resources and at the same time carry environmental issues — water level, drainage, groundwater management."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Date palms and olives are Siwa's life base. Date palm fruit is food and commodity, one reason the oasis held meaning on caravan routes. Olives and olive oil tie deeply to local food culture and economy."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Siwa, water isn't landscape but resource. Looking at springs and salt lakes, beyond beauty, seeing them as the conditions for people continuing to live in this small basin deepens place understanding."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Great Sand Sea"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Outside Siwa spreads the Great Sand Sea."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "This region of huge dunes spans Egypt and Libya as vast desert. From Siwa, 4WD tours into the dunes are common, combining sunset, stars, sandboarding, fossil-bearing strata, and desert springs."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Treat the Great Sand Sea only as attraction and you miss Siwa's meaning. With this desert, Siwa long held distinctness. With this desert, movement, trade, and life were limited."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Reach the dunes and you see how small a green exception the oasis is. Returning to town, the date palms and springs become more concrete than before."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For the desert, use trusted local guides and vehicles. Roads are often hard to see; weather and vehicle condition matter. Not a place to enter lightly alone."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's craft and memory"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa's culture isn't visible through ruins alone."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Silver jewellery, embroidery, baskets, traditional dress, and household items hold the memory of Siwa society and ritual. Women's embroidery and wedding dress, silver necklaces and bracelets carry a vocabulary different from Nile-valley craft."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "7062qxjjh4ew",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "a85ngnb59scx"
          ],
          "text": "The Siwa House museum"
        },
        {
          "_key": "v3u4ujh73vxh",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " in town is small and ethnographic; worth time. Visit before browsing market crafts and ornaments stop reading as souvenirs and read as meaning held in life and ritual."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "a85ngnb59scx",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.siwa-oasis.siwa-house-museum",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Not everything in markets is old traditional craft. Many are made for tourism, with varying quality. So before buying, hold time for the background."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Festivals and community"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa has events keeping community bonds."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Well known is the autumn Siyaha festival. Not a tourist show — an event tied to local social reconciliation and unity. Through shared meals, song, and gathering, it confirms community relations."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If travelling Siwa around then, don't approach as spectacle. Defer to local people or guide judgment on photos and participation. Siwa culture doesn't exist only to show travellers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The date harvest is also a time to feel town life. Market and field movement shifts, and Siwa as an agricultural town before tourist destination reads clearly."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "How to get there and how many days"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000065",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000064",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The basic way to Siwa is by road."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000067",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "l9z1w0f3aoo8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Direct from Cairo is a long drive. Often via Marsa Matruh on the Mediterranean coast, then south. From "
        },
        {
          "_key": "4ylvbmjrckci",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "kp0cawdsxdlu"
          ],
          "text": "Alexandria"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ei2ytk8w88d5",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " also a long road, with substantial transfer time. No rail reaches Siwa, no scheduled passenger airport."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "kp0cawdsxdlu",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58750",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000069",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000068",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Public bus, private car, or stopping at Marsa Matruh. For short trips wanting time predictability, private car or trusted arrangement is more realistic."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Including Siwa, at least two nights. One night is too short against the transfer load. To see the oracle temple, Shali, Gebel el-Mawta, salt lakes, springs, and the Great Sand Sea without strain, three nights is realistic."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When to go"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "To visit Siwa, October to April is the most workable season."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000071",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000070",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Day heat is comparatively gentle, easing town walks, site visits, and desert excursions. Winter nights cool. Don't think \"desert oasis means warm always.\""
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000073",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000072",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Summer is very hot, with limited daytime activity. For interest in date harvest or quieter periods, meaning exists; heat preparation is needed. Avoid forced daytime sightseeing."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000075",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000074",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "During Ramadan, town life rhythms shift. Restaurant and shop hours change; premise on quiet days and lively nights."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000077",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000076",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "How to include Siwa in the itinerary"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000079",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000078",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa isn't a must-include for a first short Egypt trip."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6kuofns03ej2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Without Cairo, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "kzma1zjkx1yu",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "el9lcp32e8nd"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "3o1k4donrujo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "zzfkrhpoutfb",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "u6v9qoscvvl5"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "2mj041rrc2b8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "n9e0gvkp3484",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "fshxg3zls8hz"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "184nlntdbvs2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " seen, prioritise the Nile-valley main route. Siwa is far and uses transfer time."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "el9lcp32e8nd",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "u6v9qoscvvl5",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "fshxg3zls8hz",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For people who want to see Egypt deeply as one country, Siwa carries large meaning. Here an Egypt different from pyramids and temples appears. An oasis living around water, Amazigh culture, a town protected by desert, and the memory of the oracle the ancient world's powerful sought answers from."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Siwa isn't an easy destination. So it isn't a place to consume in a hurry."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000081",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000080",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Take time, understand the land's conditions, hold distance to life — visited that way, Siwa widens Egypt's map greatly."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
